  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\frac{6}{3}).$",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{6}{3}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3!}{3!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3\\cdot 2}\\cdot \\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
